   "l": "and you return again to the limitless.",
   "v": true,
   "n": "無極, 'having no limit', is two plain words here and nothing more. Some fourteen centuries later Zhou Dunyi made it the opening term of Song cosmology — 無極而太極, 'limitless, and yet the supreme pole' — and it has been read backwards into this line ever since. 極 you met in chapter 16's 致虛極, where it was the utmost point a thing is pushed to."
  },
